{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-along-line","title":"lem:busemann-along-line","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":1020,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:busemann-along-line","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-le-approx]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:busemann-along-line","line":1628,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Busemann functions along a minimizing line]\n\\label{lem:busemann-along-line}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:busemann-function, def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\n\n\n\nFor a minimizing line $\\lambda\\colon\\Ar\\to M$, let $B_+$ and $B_-$\nbe the Busemann functions of $t\\mapsto\\lambda(t)$ and\n$t\\mapsto\\lambda(-t)$. Then\n$$B_+(\\lambda(u))=-u,qquad B_-(\\lambda(u))=u\\qquad(u\\in\\Ar).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:busemann-le-approx}\nFor $t\\ge\\max(u,0)$,\n$B_{\\lambda_+,t}(\\lambda(u))=(t-u)-t=-u$, while for all $t\\ge0$ the\nsame approximant is $|t-u|-t\\ge-u$. Apply this also to the reversed\nline.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Busemann functions along a minimizing line] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a627573656d616e6e2d616c6f6e672d6c696e65\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">morgan-tian</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Abusemann-function\">↗ def:busemann-function</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aminimizing-geodesic-window\">↗ def:minimizing-geodesic-window</a> <p></p>For a minimizing line <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda \\colon \\Ar \\to M$\">$\\lambda \\colon \\Ar \\to M$</span>, let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_+$\">$B_+$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_-$\">$B_-$</span> be the Busemann functions of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\mapsto \\lambda (t)$\">$t\\mapsto \\lambda (t)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\mapsto \\lambda (-t)$\">$t\\mapsto \\lambda (-t)$</span>. Then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ B_+(\\lambda (u))=-u,qquad B_-(\\lambda (u))=u\\qquad (u\\in \\Ar ). \\]\">\\[ B_+(\\lambda (u))=-u,qquad B_-(\\lambda (u))=u\\qquad (u\\in \\Ar ). \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-le-approx\">↗ lem:busemann-le-approx</a> For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\ge \\max (u,0)$\">$t\\ge \\max (u,0)$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_{\\lambda _+,t}(\\lambda (u))=(t-u)-t=-u$\">$B_{\\lambda _+,t}(\\lambda (u))=(t-u)-t=-u$</span>, while for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\ge 0$\">$t\\ge 0$</span> the same approximant is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|t-u|-t\\ge -u$\">$|t-u|-t\\ge -u$</span>. Apply this also to the reversed line. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#prop:parallel-gradient-splitting","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-pair-nonneg","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function","title":"def:busemann-function","label":"def:busemann-function"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-le-approx","title":"lem:busemann-le-approx","label":"lem:busemann-le-approx"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#cor:busemann-pair-vanishes-on-line","title":"cor:busemann-pair-vanishes-on-line","label":"cor:busemann-pair-vanishes-on-line"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#line","title":"line","label":"line"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-along-line","title":"lem:busemann-along-line","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Busemann functions along a minimizing line]\n\\label{lem:busemann-along-line}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:busemann-function, def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\n\n\n\nFor a minimizing line $\\lambda\\colon\\Ar\\to M$, let $B_+$ and $B_-$\nbe the Busemann functions of $t\\mapsto\\lambda(t)$ and\n$t\\mapsto\\lambda(-t)$. Then\n$$B_+(\\lambda(u))=-u,qquad B_-(\\lambda(u))=u\\qquad(u\\in\\Ar).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:busemann-le-approx}\nFor $t\\ge\\max(u,0)$,\n$B_{\\lambda_+,t}(\\lambda(u))=(t-u)-t=-u$, while for all $t\\ge0$ the\nsame approximant is $|t-u|-t\\ge-u$. Apply this also to the reversed\nline.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function","title":"def:busemann-function","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-le-approx","title":"lem:busemann-le-approx","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}